{
  "_readme": [
    "CircuitCraft catalog — seed data for the Phase-1 schema.",
    "",
    "architecture.md refers to a 30-36 SKU CircuitCraft prototype but supplies only one",
    "complete record: AeroCase Pro / CASE-IP16-BLK / 999 / quantity 20 / compatible with",
    "iphone_16 / cross-sells a screen protector (D§34). It also names a few prices in",
    "worked examples: ShieldCase Premium 1299 with stock 5 (R§10), a 30W charger at 1499",
    "with SKU CHARGER-30W (L§20, L§21), and a screen protector at 299 (L§25).",
    "",
    "Every one of those values is reproduced here exactly. The remaining products are",
    "authored, because the catalog does not exist anywhere else, and they are authored",
    "under a rule: each is a fictional CircuitCraft own-brand item described only by",
    "structural attributes - material, colour, wattage, port type, cable length, capacity,",
    "battery hours, ANC yes/no. No certifications, ratings, review counts, test results,",
    "warranty terms or real third-party brand names appear anywhere in this file.",
    "",
    "Money is a STRING, never a JSON number: json.loads would turn 999.00 into a float",
    "before any validation could intervene, and no float ever touches a price (ADR-008).",
    "",
    "The catalog is shaped so that every hard constraint in ADR-005 is individually",
    "testable: an out-of-stock variant (CASE-IP16-CLR, SLV-14-NVY), an iPhone 15 case that",
    "must be excluded from iPhone 16 searches (CASE-IP15-BLK), products either side of the",
    "1500 budget line, earbuds with no compatibility rules at all, and pixel_9 as a",
    "resolvable device with zero compatible products - which is the R§14 no-match path",
    "rather than the ADR-003 unresolvable-device path."
  ],

